{"alignments":[],"candidates":[{"additionalConceptCount":0,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. All lines in the plane, in the spatial-angle sense.","reason":"A line normal to a plane has direction perpendicular to every direction in that plane, including directions of lines not passing through its foot.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["The answer uses spatial perpendicularity by direction; some lines in the plane need not intersect the normal line."],"questionId":"cnm_h121_q3","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"definition","label":"Use the definition","methodDirectNodeIds":{"definition":["math:line-plane-perpendicular-definition"]},"nodeIds":["math:line-plane-perpendicular-definition"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 19","reason":"For the cube [0,3]^3, the plane is x+y+z=4.5. A unit cube with lower-corner coordinate sum s intersects it exactly when s≤4.5≤s+3, so s=2,3,4. Of 27 cubes, four have s≤1 and four have s≥5, leaving 19.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1995_AMC_12_Q30","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h151","cnm_p160","cnm_174"],"id":"1995_AMC_12_Q30_m1","label":"Describe the plane and count excluded cubes","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1995_AMC_12_Q30_m1":["math:lattice-counting","math:line-plane-perpendicular-definition","cnm_h154"]},"nodeIds":["math:lattice-counting","math:line-plane-perpendicular-definition","cnm_h154","cnm_h151","cnm_p160","cnm_174"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D. They are perpendicular to each other.","reason":"A plane containing a line perpendicular to another plane is perpendicular to that other plane.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_h122_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_